crDroid 16.0 variant of lineage-16/patches/packages/modules/Connectivity.patch

Only the BpfNetMaps.java part is carried. The other two files of the LineageOS
patch (bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp and bpf/netd/BpfHandler.cpp, which turn the
kernel-version gates into warnings so the 4.14 kernel does not bootloop)
are NOT needed here: crDroid's own android_packages_modules_Connectivity fork
(branch 16.0) already relaxes those same gates, and the LineageOS hunks no
longer apply to it (checked 2026-10-18, see crdroid-16/VERIFIED.md).
What remains makes the local-network-blocking BPF maps optional, so that
system_server does not throw at boot on a kernel without them.

